@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: Patcher UAT
	Testing the Patcher UAT instance.

Teardown:
	* I go to the Patcher homepage
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "${staticAccountCode}"
	* I tear down the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "${staticAccountCode}"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent3}" and type "Generated"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent3}" and type "Generated Private Public"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent3}" and type "Patch"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent}" and type "Rebase"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Rebase"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Rebase"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Rebase"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent4}" and type "Rebase"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent}" and type "Workaround"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Workaround"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Workaround"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Workaround"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent4}" and type "Workaround"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent}" and type "Patch"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Patch"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Patch"
	* I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent4}" and type "Patch"

Scenario: Create a 72 build
	@ test.group = "0"
	As a TSE, I should be able to create a 7.1 build containing private child builds

	Given I log into the Patcher homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "liferay"
	And I generate random fix content
	And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
	| Product         | DXP 7.2                                          |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210	                             |
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent}                              |
	| Branch Name     | LPP-34242                                        |
	| Github URL      | git@github.com:JavierMoral/liferay-portal-ee.git |
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent}" and type "Patch" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent} |
	| Version         | 1.0                 |
	| Product         | DXP 7.2             |        
	| Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210  |
	| Patcher Status  | Adding              |
	| Type            | Patch               |
	When I check the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent}" and type "Patch" for add completion
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent}" and type "Patch" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent}         |
	| Version         | 1.0                         |
	| Product         | DXP 7.2                     |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210          |
	| Git Hash        | bcb7100e49                  |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete                    |
	| Type            | Patch                       |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)  |
	When I generate a random ticket number
	And I create a Patcher build for a new account with the following values
	| Product         | DXP 7.2               |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210    |
	| Tickets List    | ${staticFixContent}   |
	| Account Code    | STVINTRA              |
	| Support Ticket  | ${staticTicketNumber} |
	And I set the account code "STVINTRA" as a static variable
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" with the following values
	| Type            | Official                |
	| Support Ticket  | ${staticTicketNumber}   |
	| Version         | 1.0                     |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210      |
	| Content         | 0 Fix Packs + 1 Tickets |
	| Patcher Status  | Merging                 |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build with the name "${staticFixContent}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" with the following values
	| Version         | 1.0                 |
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent} |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210  |
	| Patcher Status  | Merging Only        |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build fix with the name "${staticFixContent}" for the child build with the name "${staticFixContent}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" with the following values
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent} |
	| Version         | 1.0                 |
	| Git Hash        | bcb7100e49          |
	| Status          | Complete            |
	| Type            | Patch               |
	When I check the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" for merge completion
	And I check the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" for compile completion
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" with the following values
	| Type            | Official                       |
	| Support Ticket  | ${staticTicketNumber}          |
	| Version         | 1.0                            |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210             |
	| Content         | 0 Fix Packs + 1 Tickets        |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete                       |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat) |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)     |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build with the name "${staticFixContent}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" with the following values
	| Version         | 1.0                            |
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent}            |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210             |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete Merging Only          |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)     |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat) |

Scenario: Create and release a 71 build with public child build
	@ test.group = "1"
	As a TSE, I should be able to create and release a 7.1 build that contains a public child build

	Given I log into the Patcher homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "liferay"
	And I generate random fix content
	And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
	| Product         | DXP 7.1                                        |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110                            |
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent}                            |
	| Branch Name     | LPS-91660-DXP-7                                |
	| Github URL      | git@github.com:brianikim/liferay-portal-ee.git |
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent}" and type "Patch" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent} |
	| Version         | 1.0                 |
	| Product         | DXP 7.1             |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110 |
	| Patcher Status  | Adding              |
	| Type            | Patch               |
	When I check the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent}" and type "Patch" for add completion
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent}" and type "Patch" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent}        |
	| Version         | 1.0                        |
	| Product         | DXP 7.1                    |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110        |
	| Git Hash        | 1916d4cf71                 |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete                   |
	| Type            | Patch                      |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat) |
	When I create a request as a user with the email address "no-reply@intuitive.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_dxp_7_1                              |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Patcher Request Subject                          |
	| Description       | Patcher Request Description                      |
	| Organization Name | Intuitive Surgical-EE-IT                         |
	And I create a Patcher build for a new account with the following values
	| Product         | DXP 7.1                |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110    |
	| Tickets List    | ${staticFixContent}    |
	| Account Code    | INTUITIVE              |
	| Support Ticket  | ${staticRequestIdList} |
	And I set the account code "INTUITIVE" as a static variable
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher build for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" with the following values
	| Type            | Official                |
	| Support Ticket  | ${staticRequestIdList}  |
	| Version         | 1.0                     |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110     |
	| Content         | 0 Fix Packs + 1 Tickets |
	| Patcher Status  | Merging                 |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build with the name "${staticFixContent}" for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" with the following values
	| Version         | 1.0                 |
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent} |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110 |
	| Patcher Status  | Merging Only        |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build fix with the name "${staticFixContent}" for the child build with the name "${staticFixContent}" for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" with the following values
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent} |
	| Version         | 1.0                 |
	| Git Hash        | 1916d4cf71          |
	| Status          | Complete            |
	| Type            | Patch               |
	When I check the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" for merge completion
	And I check the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" for compile completion
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher build for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" with the following values
	| Type            | Official                       |
	| Support Ticket  | ${staticRequestIdList}         |
	| Version         | 1.0                            |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110            |
	| Content         | 0 Fix Packs + 1 Tickets        |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete                       |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat) |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)     |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build with the name "${staticFixContent}" for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" with the following values
	| Version         | 1.0                                   |
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent}                   |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110                   |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete Merging Only                 |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat)        |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)            |
	When I release a Patcher build for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE"
	Then the ticket with the ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the comment containing the text "liferay-hotfix-"
	And the ticket with the ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the comment containing the text "-7110.zip"

Scenario: Create a public MP build
	@ test.group = "2"
	As a TSE, I should be able to create a public MP build

	Given I log into the Patcher homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "liferay"
	And I generate random fix content for the first fix
	And I generate random fix content for the second fix
	And I generate random fix content for the third fix
	And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
	| Product         | DXP 7.0 Liferay Knowledge Base               |
	| Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010        |
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent1}                         |
	| Branch Name     | LPS-87103                                    |
	| Github URL      | git@github.com:IstvanD/liferay-portal-ee.git |
	And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
	| Product         | DXP 7.0 Liferay Knowledge Base                   |
	| Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010            |
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent2}                             |
	| Branch Name     | LPP-32185-hotfix                                 |
	| Github URL      | git@github.com:kenduenwald/liferay-portal-ee.git |
	| Workaround      | true                                             |
	And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
	| Product         | DXP 7.0 Liferay Knowledge Base                  |
	| Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010           |
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent3}                            |
	| Branch Name     | LPS-91303-marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010 |
	| Github URL      | git@github.com:IstvanD/liferay-portal-ee.git    |
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent1}                  |
	| Version         | 1.0                                   |
	| Product         | DXP 7.0 Liferay Knowledge Base        |
	| Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010 |
	| Patcher Status  | Adding                                |
	| Type            | Patch                                 |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Workaround" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent2}                  |
	| Version         | 1.0                                   |
	| Product         | DXP 7.0 Liferay Knowledge Base        |
	| Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010 |
	| Patcher Status  | Adding                                |
	| Type            | Workaround                            |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Patch" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent3}                  |
	| Version         | 1.0                                   |
	| Product         | DXP 7.0 Liferay Knowledge Base        |
	| Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010 |
	| Patcher Status  | Adding                                |
	| Type            | Patch                                 |
	When I check the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch" for add completion
	When I check the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Workaround" for add completion
	When I check the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Patch" for add completion
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent1}                  |
	| Version         | 1.0                                   |
	| Product         | DXP 7.0 Liferay Knowledge Base        |
	| Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010 |
	| Git Hash        | 2a6c623d8f                            |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete                              |
	| Type            | Patch                                 |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)            |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Workaround" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent2}                  |
	| Version         | 1.0                                   |
	| Product         | DXP 7.0 Liferay Knowledge Base        |
	| Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010 |
	| Git Hash        | 9d14076367                            |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete                              |
	| Type            | Workaround                            |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)            |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Patch" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent3}                  |
	| Version         | 1.0                                   |
	| Product         | DXP 7.0 Liferay Knowledge Base        |
	| Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010 |
	| Git Hash        | 2a607f48e1                            |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete                              |
	| Type            | Patch                                 |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)            |
	When I generate a random ticket number
	And I create a Patcher build for a new account with the following values
	| Product         | DXP 7.0 Liferay Knowledge Base                                 |
	| Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010                          |
	| Tickets List    | ${staticFixContent1},${staticFixContent2},${staticFixContent3} |
	| Account Code    | INDIANIOCLCM                                                   |
	| Support Ticket  | ${staticTicketNumber}                                          |
	And I set the account code "INDIANIOCLCM" as a static variable
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "INDIANIOCLCM" with the following values
	| Type            | Official                              |
	| Support Ticket  | ${staticTicketNumber}                 |
	| Version         | 1.0                                   |
	| Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010 |
	| Content         | 0 Fix Packs + 3 Tickets               |
	| Patcher Status  | Merging                               |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "INDIANIOCLCM" with the following values
	| Version         | 1.0                                                              |
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3} |
	| Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010                            |
	| Patcher Status  | Merging Only                                                     |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build fix with the name "${staticFixContent1}" for the child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "INDIANIOCLCM" with the following values
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent1} |
	| Version         | 1.0                  |
	| Git Hash        | 2a6c623d8f           |
	| Status          | Complete             |
	| Type            | Patch                |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build fix with the name "${staticFixContent2}" for the child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "INDIANIOCLCM" with the following values
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent2} |
	| Version         | 1.0                  |
	| Git Hash        | 9d14076367           |
	| Status          | Complete             |
	| Type            | Workaround           |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build fix with the name "${staticFixContent3}" for the child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "INDIANIOCLCM" with the following values
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent3} |
	| Version         | 1.0                  |
	| Git Hash        | 2a607f48e1           |
	| Status          | Complete             |
	| Type            | Patch                |
	When I check the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "INDIANIOCLCM" for merge completion
	And I check the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "INDIANIOCLCM" for compile completion
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "INDIANIOCLCM" with the following values
	| Type            | Official                              |
	| Support Ticket  | ${staticTicketNumber}                 |
	| Version         | 1.0                                   |
	| Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010 |
	| Content         | 0 Fix Packs + 3 Tickets               |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete                              |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat)        |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)            |
	And I should be able to view a Patcher child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "INDIANIOCLCM" with the following values
	| Version         | 1.0                                                              |
	| Name            | ${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3} |
	| Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010                            |
	| Patcher Status  | Complete Merging Only                                            |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat)                                   |
	| Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)                                       |

Scenario: Create a private MP build
