Scenario: Create a 71 build with public and private child builds
	@ test.group = "4"
	As a TSE, I should be able to create a 7.1 build containing both public and private child builds

	Given I log into the Patcher homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "liferay"
	And I generate random fix content for the first fix
	And I generate random fix content for the second fix
	And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
	| Product         | DXP 7.1                                             |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-8-7110-private                         |
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent1}                                |
	| Branch Name     | fix-pack-LPP-33279-dxp-8-private                    |
	| Github URL      | git@github.com:jonathanmccann/liferay-portal-ee.git |
	And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
	| Product         | DXP 7.1                                              |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-4-7110                                  |
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent2}                                 |
	| Branch Name     | LPS-89633-dxp-4                                      |
	| Github URL      | git@github.com:gregory-bretall/liferay-portal-ee.git |
	| Workaround      | true                                                 |
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	Then I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch" with the following values
	| Content         | ${staticFixContent1}        |
	| Version         | 1.0                         |
	| Product         | DXP 7.1                     |
	| Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-8-7110-private |
	| Patcher Status  | Adding                      |
	| Type            | Patch                       |
